<img alt="[Cheonji Ilbo = Reporter Park Jun-seong] Choi Kyung-ho, full-time professor at Kangwon National University Industry-Academia Cooperation Center (PhD in Brain Engineering), is giving a keynote speech on the theme of ‘Humanity’s Attitude for Sustainable AI Utilization’ at the ‘3rd Smart AI Forum’ held at the Korea Press Center International Conference Hall in Jung-gu, Seoul on the afternoon of the 16th. ⓒCheonji Ilbo 2025.05.16." src="https://www.newscj.com/news/photo/202505/3270630_3335017_1550.jpg" />
[Cheonji Ilbo = Reporter Park Jun-seong] Choi Kyung-ho, full-time professor at Kangwon National University Industry-Academia Cooperation Center (PhD in Brain Engineering), is giving a keynote speech on the theme of &lsquo;Humanity&rsquo;s Attitude for Sustainable AI Utilization&rsquo; at the &lsquo;3rd Smart AI Forum&rsquo; held at the Korea Press Center International Conference Hall in Jung-gu, Seoul on the afternoon of the 16th. ⓒCheonji Ilbo 2025.05.16.



[Cheonji Ilbo = Reporter Hwang Hae-yeon] &ldquo;The answer for sustainable AI utilization is ethics. I think if the Republic of Korea establishes an AI Ethics Federal Government first and reigns over the world, and also creates a monitoring body within it, we can create a Republic of Korea that leads humanity and can prosper together with technology.&rdquo;

Choi Kyung-ho, full-time professor at Kangwon National University Industry-Academia Cooperation Center (PhD in Brain Engineering), stated this at the &lsquo;3rd Smart AI Forum&rsquo; hosted by the national daily newspaper Cheonji Ilbo (CEO Lee Sang-myeon) at the Korea Press Center International Conference Hall in Jung-gu, Seoul on the 16th.

This forum was held under the theme of &lsquo;The Era of Great AI Transformation, the Spirit of the Times and Humanity&rsquo;s Attitude - Focusing on Human-Centered AI Utilization and the Role of Humanity&rsquo;.

Professor Choi delivered the second keynote speech on the theme of &lsquo;Humanity&rsquo;s Attitude for Sustainable AI Utilization&rsquo;.

He said, &ldquo;I&rsquo;ve been using AI for 25 years, and looking at it now, there is more development in AI and semiconductors overseas. So, questions like &lsquo;Is there any area where we can intervene?&rsquo; and &lsquo;Can we provide direction to our children with technology?&rsquo; come to mind.&rdquo;

He continued, &ldquo;Just like companies and parents, if you ask, &lsquo;Will all our jobs disappear at some point and we&rsquo;ll become subordinate to the US?&rsquo; or &lsquo;What kind of jobs can we have?&rsquo;, the answer is &lsquo;ethics&rsquo;,&rdquo; he emphasized.

Professor Choi explained, &ldquo;There are a lot of algorithm bias issues. There are many people who are starting to use deepfakes extensively because they can manipulate celebrity photos or create videos to attract attention and make money.&rdquo;

He added that social discrimination is being reinforced due to algorithmic bias, such as facial recognition AI misidentifying people of color or hiring AI favoring male applicants.


<img alt="[Cheonji Ilbo = Reporter Park Jun-seong] Choi Kyung-ho, full-time professor at Kangwon National University Industry-Academia Cooperation Center (PhD in Brain Engineering), is giving a keynote speech on the theme of ‘Humanity’s Attitude for Sustainable AI Utilization’ at the ‘3rd Smart AI Forum’ held at the Korea Press Center International Conference Hall in Jung-gu, Seoul on the afternoon of the 16th. ⓒCheonji Ilbo 2025.05.16." src="https://www.newscj.com/news/photo/202505/3270630_3335018_1638.jpg" />
[Cheonji Ilbo = Reporter Park Jun-seong] Choi Kyung-ho, full-time professor at Kangwon National University Industry-Academia Cooperation Center (PhD in Brain Engineering), is giving a keynote speech on the theme of &lsquo;Humanity&rsquo;s Attitude for Sustainable AI Utilization&rsquo; at the &lsquo;3rd Smart AI Forum&rsquo; held at the Korea Press Center International Conference Hall in Jung-gu, Seoul on the afternoon of the 16th. ⓒCheonji Ilbo 2025.05.16.



Furthermore, Professor Choi mentioned that as AI causes changes such as the disappearance of some jobs and the creation of new opportunities, corporations and the government must fulfill their social responsibility. He said that everyone should be helped to adapt to the AI era through AI education and retraining programs, and AI should not be developed merely as a tool to make money, but in a sustainable direction.

Professor Choi cited the case of Volkswagen&rsquo;s &lsquo;Digital Academy&rsquo; implemented in Germany in 2020. As Volkswagen transitioned from traditional car manufacturing to electric vehicles and AI-based production, they provided new technical training to their employees.

Professor Choi said, &ldquo;Current AI is so fast that it doesn&rsquo;t give us time to control or judge, compared to existing technologies. I also have many concerns about whether we can control AI.&rdquo;

He added, &ldquo;If certain technologies, under the guise of ethics and under the guise of common prosperity for humanity, create standard technologies and say we must follow these technologies, there is a high possibility that we will become subordinate to them. But we cannot lead 100%.&rdquo;

Professor Choi asserted, &ldquo;To create good AI, we must think ethically, take responsibility for society, and develop it with people at the center. Above all, our perspective on technology must change. AI is not just a tool, but a test that shows us what kind of future we want.&rdquo;

